{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/31209","id":276391661,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNzYzOTE2NjE=","number":31209,"title":"The construct \"where.not\" doesn't respect boolean algebra","user":{"login":"fterrazzoni","id":5654121,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTQxMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5654121?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni","html_url":"https://github.com/fterrazzoni","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fterrazzoni/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":107191,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDcxOTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/labels/activerecord","name":"activerecord","color":"0b02e1","default":false,"description":null},{"id":12449438,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMjQ0OTQzOA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/labels/stale","name":"stale","color":"444444","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":24,"created_at":"2017-11-23T14:18:49Z","updated_at":"2023-09-30T15:54:47Z","closed_at":"2018-06-02T09:07:22Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nWhen two predicates A and B are given to a `where` clause, Rails combines them using `AND`, which is the expected behavior. \r\n```ruby\r\nModel.where(col1: 1, col2: 2).to_sql\r\n\r\n# => SELECT \"models\".* FROM \"models\" WHERE \"models\".\"col1\" = 1 AND \"models\".\"col2\" = 2\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen the clause is negated (using `where.not`), Rails distributes the `NOT` to every predicate before combining them using `AND`. Why? \r\n\r\n```ruby\r\nModel.where.not(col1: 1, col2: 2).to_sql\r\n\r\n# => SELECT \"models\".* FROM \"models\" WHERE (\"models\".\"col1\" != 1) AND (\"models\".\"col2\" != 2)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`NOT(A AND B)` = `NOT(A) OR NOT(B)` \r\n\r\nIn my example, the query should look like:\r\n```sql\r\nSELECT \"models\".* FROM \"models\" WHERE (\"models\".\"col1\" != 1) OR (\"models\".\"col2\" != 2)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`NOT(A AND B)` = `NOT(A) AND NOT(B)` (wrong)\r\n\r\nIt's worth noting that the correct behavior can still be obtained by writing SQL directly:\r\n\r\n```ruby\r\nModel.where.not('\"models\".\"col1\" = 1 AND \"models\".\"col2\" = 2').to_sql\r\n# => SELECT \"models\".* FROM \"models\" WHERE (NOT (\"models\".\"col1\" = 1 AND \"models\".\"col2\" = 2))\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt makes the construct `where.not(...)` behave very differently depending on the kind of arguments which are passed to it.\r\n\r\nThe culprit seems to be located here : https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/be81b5066074fee8126144d072c6132b93d1fe39/activerecord/lib/active_record/relation/where_clause.rb#L74\r\n\r\n### System configuration\r\n**Rails version**: 5.1.4\r\n\r\n**Ruby version**: MRI 2.4.2\r\n ","closed_by":{"login":"rails-bot[bot]","id":28418009,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mjg0MTgwMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2272?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/rails-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rails-bot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209/reactions","total_count":20,"+1":11,"-1":4,"laugh":3,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/31209/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}